{
  "_doc": "Permission ledger — single source of truth for what Bash may auto-run. Read by .claude/scripts/bash_permission_gate.py (PreToolUse) and appended to by .claude/scripts/permission_recorder.py (PostToolUse) when the user grants a prompt. allow_keys: token-prefix -> note. allow_patterns: regex allowed at segment level. ask_patterns + denials: regex that always forces a human prompt. grants: auto-recorded user approvals — empty on a fresh clone; this ledger carries only the portable seeds, and per-machine grants accrue locally as you approve prompts.",
